A||||8||BOILERMAKER||Installation of a 3300||||1
Z||000000||BOILERMAKER||10-20-1999||07:26 PM||||I just found a Grand Prix that was demolished except for the front of the car.  This car just so happened to have a 3300 in it.  I want it, but am curious if the 3300 will sit in my engine compartment with little modifications.  <P>Will the mounts have to be changed?<P>Will the 2.8 computer work with this 3300?<P>Do I need to change the whole wiring harnesses?<P>The grand prix was a later model (early 90's I am purely guessing).<P>I will check tomorrow on the price to haul that puppy on home, but need some information if anybody has any.||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||10-20-1999||09:04 PM||||&gt;I just found a Grand Prix that was demolished except for the front of the car. This car just so happened to have a 3300 in it. I want it, but am curious if the 3300 will sit in my engine compartment with little modifications. <P>*The mods are average. It will sit on the cradle but the exhaust will need to be custom to the cat. A few other little details.<P>&gt;Will the mounts have to be changed?<BR>*Yes.<P>&gt;Will the 2.8 computer work with this 3300?<BR>*No.<P>&gt;Do I need to change the whole wiring harnesses?<BR>*Whole harness? No. Some of it? Yes.<P>Still might be worth it if the price is right. Much more torque at the low end.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||BOILERMAKER||10-20-1999||09:32 PM||||I take it that you have changed this engine out already???  If so, it might be a good idea to get in touch with you, or someone who has done this, to get a better idea of what has to be done.  I am really interested in doing this.  <P>It won't be an over-the-weekend job I know, I am going to take my time and hopefully get it in by this spring if possible.||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||10-21-1999||12:28 AM||||I own an 86 SE V6 Fiero and I've swapped a Buick SC into my Ciera GT. The 3300 for swap purposes is the same engine. 90% of the Ciera swap will apply to the Fiero. I've considered doing the swap into the Fiero.<P>Are you going to use a manual or auto trans?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||BOILERMAKER||10-21-1999||09:05 AM||||I am going to be using the manual getrag 5spd on the engine.  This was another question that I had whether this would work or not.  <BR>You mentioned the Ciera, but what about the Grand Prix??  Is this the same engine.  I am getting ready to call the boneyard in a bit and find out on the moneys.||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||10-21-1999||10:06 AM||||All of the Buicks are essentially the same. The primary difference (physically) is the oil filter housing. That *might* need changing depending on the engine. There are different version available from different cars.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||BOILERMAKER||10-21-1999||12:23 PM||||OK, around $350 for the engine.  He won't sell me the whole thing, so I also need the wiring harness and computer.  If I can get them to take the whole thing out without screwing anything up that would be good, but...<P>How does this sound?  Would I be better off with just upgrading my 2.8 to a 3.1?||||reg||1
Z||000007||terryk||10-21-1999||03:03 PM||||It's a matter of labor. Figure that the car will be down 1 month to do the swap. That's figuring 100 hours of work roughly (not including beer breaks). <P>Putting the 3300 in is not the same as rebuildng the 2.8L and installing it (in effort.)<P>However, if you are committed to the swap, it leaves a lot of room for future improvements.<BR> <BR>The four key items are harness/ECM, exhaust, oil filter, and flywheel. <P>If the 3300 is torque axis mounted, the oil filter adapter may need to change<P>You will need to work out a flywheel. I think the N car 3.0L came with a manual trans. If not, you will need to fabricate/modify some other application to work. It's been done though.<P>The 3300 exhaust is a wrap around system and will exit at the rear of the car on the trunk side. A new pipe will be needed to go from there back over the trans and to the cat. Unless you plan on some major exhaust fabricate, this will be necessary.<P>The 3300 ECM (or one of the later 3.8L ECM's) will be needed.<P>I assume you don't have emissions testing where you are at....<P>Scared off yet?<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 10-21-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||BOILERMAKER||10-21-1999||03:49 PM||||I am not scared off yet.  In fact, I am kind of relieved about the exhaust.  It sounds like a lot less piping is needed.  I mainly need to go out there and take a look at the engine again to see what I can see.<P>Thanks for the info.  I am sure that I will have more questions in the near future.||||reg||1
